{
  "name": "TestOutputWriteHasNoSpuriousChannel",
  "comment": "Drift case 1 — the load-bearing reason this branch exists.\n\nStep text `- write out %message%` (from test/Simple/Start.goal:5) carries no\nchannel clause. With per-action notes (os/system/modules/output/write.notes.md)\ncarrying the channel routing rule only when output.write is in the planner's\nset, the LLM should emit:\nparameters: { Data: %message% }   (no channel key)\n\nPre-fix shape this test forbids:\nany 'channel' parameter on output.write when step text had no channel clause\n\nRead .pr requires copying to a .txt first because '.pr' MIME deserializes to a\nGoal object, defeating substring assertions. Copy → read as text → assert.\nThe companion C# test PLang.Tests/Builder/CompilePromptTests/DriftCaseArtifactTests.cs\ndoes the structural check on the parsed Goal — both layers guard the same fact.\n\nArchitect's 3-fresh-cache verification rule runs externally:\nrm -rf test/Simple/.build\nPlangConsole/bin/Debug/net10.0/plang build /test/Simple   # then plang --test (x3)",
  "step": [
